{"type":"standard","title":"Chris Jones (Arkansas politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Chris Jones (Arkansas politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q115173915","titles":{"canonical":"Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)","normalized":"Chris Jones (Arkansas politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Chris Jones (Arkansas politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":71719322,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Chris_Jones_Congressional_Campaign.jpg/330px-Chris_Jones_Congressional_Campaign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":220},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6e/Chris_Jones_Congressional_Campaign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":600,"height":400},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378354800","tid":"f8cbb151-bf9f-11f1-81bc-825464a60183","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:02:02Z","description":"American politician (born 1976)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Chris_Jones_(Arkansas_politician)"}},"extract":"Christopher Michael Jones is an American politician and the Democratic nominee for Congressional District 02. He was the Democratic Party nominee for governor of Arkansas in the 2022 election. Born in Pine Bluff, Arkansas, he attended Morehouse College and graduate school at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. He's currently the Director of Community and Social Innovation with BCT Partners. He previously worked at the Arkansas Regional Innovation Hub, from which he resigned in April 2021. On June 15, 2021, Jones announced that he was entering the Democratic primary for governor of Arkansas. He won the primary but lost the general election to Sarah Huckabee Sanders. On August 1, 2025, Jones filed to run for the Democratic nomination in Arkansas's 2nd congressional district.","extract_html":"<p><b>Christopher Michael Jones</b> is an American politician and the Democratic nominee for Congressional District 02. He was the Democratic Party nominee for governor of Arkansas in the 2022 election. Born in Pine Bluff, Arkansas, he attended Morehouse College and graduate school at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. He's currently the Director of Community and Social Innovation with BCT Partners. He previously worked at the Arkansas Regional Innovation Hub, from which he resigned in April 2021. On June 15, 2021, Jones announced that he was entering the Democratic primary for governor of Arkansas. He won the primary but lost the general election to Sarah Huckabee Sanders. On August 1, 2025, Jones filed to run for the Democratic nomination in Arkansas's 2nd congressional district.</p>"}